1
00:00:16,938 --> 00:00:18,021
[whoops]

2
00:00:25,521 --> 00:00:27,771
[whooshes]

3
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:31,896
- [humming]
- [grunts]

4
00:00:37,146 --> 00:00:38,395
[both grunting]

5
00:00:38,396 --> 00:00:40,188
[laughs hysterically]

6
00:00:54,229 --> 00:00:56,229
[intriguing music playing]

7
00:01:00,063 --> 00:01:02,270
Well, kid, ready for our assignment?

8
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:03,395
[laughing gleefully]

9
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:05,437
Look, if you're gonna be a bounty hunter,

10
00:01:05,438 --> 00:01:07,770
you'll have to sound more intimidating
than that.

11
00:01:07,771 --> 00:01:08,853
[clears throat]

12
00:01:08,854 --> 00:01:10,396
[laughs wickedly]

13
00:01:11,146 --> 00:01:13,854
[sighs] Coruscant wasn't built in a day.

14
00:01:14,396 --> 00:01:15,728
Let's go meet our contact.

15
00:01:15,729 --> 00:01:16,979
[hums]

16
00:01:18,521 --> 00:01:20,062
[whoops]

17
00:01:20,063 --> 00:01:21,438
[Mando] Be careful in here.

18
00:01:21,563 --> 00:01:23,062
We have powerful enemies.

19
00:01:23,063 --> 00:01:25,603
Like those pirates we ran out of Nevarro.

20
00:01:25,604 --> 00:01:27,770
So stay alert.
We don't want any--

21
00:01:27,771 --> 00:01:29,603
- [all] Surprise!
- [Mando] Ahh!

22
00:01:29,604 --> 00:01:31,438
[all screaming]

23
00:01:38,396 --> 00:01:39,438
Suprise?

24
00:01:40,854 --> 00:01:41,937
Peli!

25
00:01:41,938 --> 00:01:43,312
What are you doing here?

26
00:01:43,313 --> 00:01:46,520
I'm supposed to meet a contact
for an important assignment.

27
00:01:46,521 --> 00:01:48,520
Your contact was Peli.

28
00:01:48,521 --> 00:01:53,645
<i>Hey Mando, I got a big time
bounty-huntin' job for you, see?</i>

29
00:01:53,646 --> 00:01:56,937
<i>And bring that cute kid with you too, see?</i>

30
00:01:56,938 --> 00:01:58,521
<i>Uh, hey, get out of the shot!</i>

31
00:01:58,854 --> 00:01:59,937
[clears throat]

32
00:01:59,938 --> 00:02:03,104
<i>And I ain't Peli Motto in disguise, see?</i>

33
00:02:03,896 --> 00:02:05,312
Wait. You?

34
00:02:05,313 --> 00:02:06,728
Were Tough-o Guy-o?

35
00:02:06,729 --> 00:02:09,145
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
But it's all good because you came!

36
00:02:09,146 --> 00:02:11,437
Now we can have this party
with all your friends.

37
00:02:11,438 --> 00:02:14,813
And we can show you how much we appreciate
everything you've done for us.

38
00:02:15,979 --> 00:02:17,063
We're leaving.

39
00:02:17,646 --> 00:02:22,062
Mando, you are gonna have fun today
whether you have fun or not.

40
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:25,895
You Mandalorians all say,
"This is the way".

41
00:02:25,896 --> 00:02:29,228
Well, for today,
this is the way, right, buddy?

42
00:02:29,229 --> 00:02:32,354
[intriguing music playing]

43
00:02:37,979 --> 00:02:39,937
[Mando sighs deeply]

44
00:02:39,938 --> 00:02:42,270
- [all cheering]
- Let's party!

45
00:02:42,271 --> 00:02:45,188
[upbeat music playing]

46
00:02:47,646 --> 00:02:50,437
Mando, where did you get
all these friends?

47
00:02:50,438 --> 00:02:52,312
I thought you kept to yourself?

48
00:02:52,313 --> 00:02:53,812
Oh, he did.

49
00:02:53,813 --> 00:02:58,895
Din Djarin here was the loneliest loner
who ever loned.

50
00:02:58,896 --> 00:03:01,145
- Till that kid came along.
- [all exclaiming]

51
00:03:01,146 --> 00:03:03,187
It's one heck of a tale!

52
00:03:03,188 --> 00:03:05,270
I don't like to talk about myself.

53
00:03:05,271 --> 00:03:07,228
Well, good thing I do!

54
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:08,478
Gather around, everyone.

55
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,103
I'll tell you the exciting story

56
00:03:10,104 --> 00:03:13,728
of how a little green kid
turned a stone-cold bounty hunter

57
00:03:13,729 --> 00:03:16,728
into a warm and fuzzy
stone-cold bounty hunter.

58
00:03:16,729 --> 00:03:19,770
How could you tell our story?

59
00:03:19,771 --> 00:03:22,103
You were only there for a tiny part of it.

60
00:03:22,104 --> 00:03:23,937
I'm a mechanic at a spaceport.

61
00:03:23,938 --> 00:03:25,978
Everybody tells me everything.

62
00:03:25,979 --> 00:03:30,478
So, the way I hear it,
is it all went down like this.

63
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:32,937
<i>Mando had just come back
from some bounty-hunting</i>

64
00:03:32,938 --> 00:03:35,646
<i>with a ship
full of captured bad guys on ice.</i>

65
00:03:36,188 --> 00:03:39,854
<i>This day, Mando got the assignment
that would change his life.</i>

66
00:03:40,313 --> 00:03:43,353
The Mandalorian, meet your new client.

67
00:03:43,354 --> 00:03:45,812
He is called The Client.

68
00:03:45,813 --> 00:03:48,353
- [sniffs]
- That's it? The Client?

69
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:52,021
Yes, we share the same first name, "The".

70
00:03:52,479 --> 00:03:54,937
Dr. Pershing, and I desire for you

71
00:03:54,938 --> 00:03:58,645
to go to Arvala-7
and acquire an asset for us.

72
00:03:58,646 --> 00:04:00,603
This asset is called--

73
00:04:00,604 --> 00:04:02,062
The Asset?

74
00:04:02,063 --> 00:04:05,312
Your powers of perspicacity
are remarkable.

75
00:04:05,313 --> 00:04:09,062
Now, I cannot divulge
the asset's identity to you,

76
00:04:09,063 --> 00:04:13,270
nor tell you its height,
color or shape of its ears.

77
00:04:13,271 --> 00:04:16,270
I can only say it is 50 years old,

78
00:04:16,271 --> 00:04:21,062
which, by any measure, you and I go by,
is quite old.

79
00:04:21,063 --> 00:04:22,895
Why did you say that so weird?

80
00:04:22,896 --> 00:04:26,062
I did it... for reasons.

81
00:04:26,063 --> 00:04:27,853
Here is your first payment.

82
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:32,687
Something Mandalorians greatly treasure,
Beskar steel.

83
00:04:32,688 --> 00:04:34,895
When you deliver the asset to me,

84
00:04:34,896 --> 00:04:38,895
there will be much more
from where that came from.

85
00:04:38,896 --> 00:04:39,896
- [crashes]
- [screams]

86
00:04:40,479 --> 00:04:42,062
[Peli] <i>So Mando took the Beskar</i>

87
00:04:42,063 --> 00:04:47,645
<i>to the last refuge of the Mandalorians
on Nevarro, the forge of The Armorer.</i>

88
00:04:47,646 --> 00:04:49,313
- [hissing]
- [clangs]

89
00:04:53,396 --> 00:04:54,978
[Armorer] For you.

90
00:04:54,979 --> 00:04:58,270
This is the Way.

91
00:04:58,271 --> 00:05:01,645
Now I must go
and fulfill my bounty-hunting contract.

92
00:05:01,646 --> 00:05:02,771
This is the Way.

93
00:05:03,563 --> 00:05:05,895
Can you show me where the door is?

94
00:05:05,896 --> 00:05:07,562
This is the Way.

95
00:05:07,563 --> 00:05:12,354
Wait. Are you saying this is the way out,
or just "This is the Way"?

96
00:05:13,854 --> 00:05:15,770
- This is the Way.
- Ugh.

97
00:05:15,771 --> 00:05:17,770
I'll find the exit on my own.

98
00:05:17,771 --> 00:05:20,562
[Peli] <i>To capture his bounty,
Mando went to Arvala-7.</i>

99
00:05:20,563 --> 00:05:25,270
It's a desolate planet, but way classier
than the other six Arvalas, oof!

100
00:05:25,271 --> 00:05:29,020
<i>There, he was aided
by a wise Ugnaught named Kuiil</i>

101
00:05:29,021 --> 00:05:31,438
{\an8}<i>who led him
to where The Asset was being held.</i>

102
00:05:32,854 --> 00:05:34,438
{\an8}Ugh, pirates.

103
00:05:36,271 --> 00:05:38,562
{\an8}I command you to produce the asset.

104
00:05:38,563 --> 00:05:40,937
And a competing bounty droid.

105
00:05:40,938 --> 00:05:42,104
- [gun cocking]
- [gunfire]

106
00:05:45,229 --> 00:05:46,813
Who's a showoff.

107
00:05:51,771 --> 00:05:53,854
That-- That droid was doing the robot.

108
00:05:55,521 --> 00:05:56,771
[grunting]

109
00:05:58,313 --> 00:05:59,479
[grunts]

110
00:06:00,521 --> 00:06:02,812
[Peli] <i>Mando fought his way
to the fortress</i>

111
00:06:02,813 --> 00:06:07,813
<i>and convinced that deadly droid
to work with him and split the reward.</i>

112
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:11,728
We're surrounded,
but I think we can beat these guys.

113
00:06:11,729 --> 00:06:15,895
[Droid] Negative. My manufacturer
protocols dictate I cannot be captured.

114
00:06:15,896 --> 00:06:18,645
Initiating self-destruct sequencing.

115
00:06:18,646 --> 00:06:19,853
Don't self-destruct!

116
00:06:19,854 --> 00:06:21,603
- Are you nuts?
- [soldier grunts]

117
00:06:21,604 --> 00:06:23,062
My sanity has been questioned.

118
00:06:23,063 --> 00:06:26,063
- Initiating self-destruct sequencing.
- [alarm blaring]

119
00:06:26,479 --> 00:06:28,270
Stop it, you crazy hunk of junk.

120
00:06:28,271 --> 00:06:29,978
You have called me a nasty name.

121
00:06:29,979 --> 00:06:31,896
- Initiating self--
- [grunts]

122
00:06:32,479 --> 00:06:34,604
[Peli] <i>Things went on like that for a bit.</i>

123
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:38,020
[Droid] It might rain later,
initiating, so--

124
00:06:38,021 --> 00:06:39,937
That's enough!

125
00:06:39,938 --> 00:06:40,938
Uh-oh!

126
00:06:41,771 --> 00:06:43,021
[explosion]

127
00:06:44,854 --> 00:06:47,395
Let's get this 50-year-old asset.

128
00:06:47,396 --> 00:06:50,354
[device beeping]

129
00:06:54,063 --> 00:06:56,145
It's just a kid.

130
00:06:56,146 --> 00:06:58,188
[Droid] I am programmed to terminate.

131
00:07:00,688 --> 00:07:01,770
[gunshot]

132
00:07:01,771 --> 00:07:02,937
No.

133
00:07:02,938 --> 00:07:04,104
[thudding]

134
00:07:09,271 --> 00:07:13,145
[Peli] <i>Mando's tough shell
cracked a teensy bit that day,</i>

135
00:07:13,146 --> 00:07:18,062
but there was one little problem
in bringing the kid back to the client.

136
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:20,603
<i>Well, actually,
a whole bunch of little problems.</i>

137
00:07:20,604 --> 00:07:23,604
[all whooping]

138
00:07:25,146 --> 00:07:27,812
My ship! I just had it waxed.

139
00:07:27,813 --> 00:07:33,020
[Peli] <i>Kuiil talked to the Jawas, and he
got them to promise to fix Mando's ship</i>

140
00:07:33,021 --> 00:07:38,687
<i>if he fought a beast called a mudhorn
and got one of its precious eggs.</i>

141
00:07:38,688 --> 00:07:39,688
[Mando grunts]

142
00:07:41,438 --> 00:07:43,188
[grunting]

143
00:07:47,146 --> 00:07:48,896
[Jawas whooping]

144
00:07:49,813 --> 00:07:50,895
[coos]

145
00:07:50,896 --> 00:07:53,853
Yeah, I like you, too,
but this is no time to be adorable.

146
00:07:53,854 --> 00:07:54,854
[roars]

147
00:07:58,313 --> 00:07:59,646
[swishing]

148
00:08:03,188 --> 00:08:04,771
[mudhorn grunts]

149
00:08:07,979 --> 00:08:13,103
[Mando] It's like he's moving that thing
with some kind of unseen force.

150
00:08:13,104 --> 00:08:15,645
It is called the Force.

151
00:08:15,646 --> 00:08:18,520
They have got to work
on better names for stuff.

152
00:08:18,521 --> 00:08:20,604
[exhilarating instrumental music playing]

153
00:08:21,771 --> 00:08:22,895
[mudhorn grunts]

154
00:08:22,896 --> 00:08:24,021
[whooping triumphantly]

155
00:08:31,854 --> 00:08:33,063
[laughs]

156
00:08:33,521 --> 00:08:35,978
[Peli] <i>With the kid's help,
Mando got the egg...</i>

157
00:08:35,979 --> 00:08:37,645
[speaking in foreign language]

158
00:08:37,646 --> 00:08:39,312
<i>...and his ship back.</i>

159
00:08:39,313 --> 00:08:41,646
[speaking in foreign language]

160
00:08:45,979 --> 00:08:47,646
[Mando] Ooh-Teeny.

161
00:08:51,396 --> 00:08:56,603
[Peli] <i>So Mando took the kid back
to the client to fulfill his assignment.</i>

162
00:08:56,604 --> 00:08:58,062
[both] Aww!

163
00:08:58,063 --> 00:09:00,937
Cease that! We are Imperial Remnants.

164
00:09:00,938 --> 00:09:02,687
We do not "aww"!

165
00:09:02,688 --> 00:09:03,812
[both] Aww!

166
00:09:03,813 --> 00:09:06,728
Stop it. Here is
your payment, Mandalorian.

167
00:09:06,729 --> 00:09:10,937
Now you may take one last
wistful look at the adorable child

168
00:09:10,938 --> 00:09:14,479
before we do terrible,
horrible, painful things to it.

169
00:09:16,646 --> 00:09:17,812
[whimpers]

170
00:09:17,813 --> 00:09:20,104
[somber instrumental music playing]

171
00:09:21,271 --> 00:09:22,437
No!

172
00:09:22,438 --> 00:09:26,395
[Peli] <i>All of a sudden,
Mando had the X Empire after him.</i>

173
00:09:26,396 --> 00:09:29,187
<i>The hunter was now the hunted,</i>

174
00:09:29,188 --> 00:09:32,437
<i>and then the most exciting thing happened.</i>

175
00:09:32,438 --> 00:09:34,353
- They met me!
- [laughs]

176
00:09:34,354 --> 00:09:35,937
[grunts]

177
00:09:35,938 --> 00:09:37,228
[Peli] <i>The end!</i>

178
00:09:37,229 --> 00:09:38,771
- [Jawas cheering]
- [giggles]

179
00:09:41,354 --> 00:09:42,937
[Mando] Wait, wait, stop.

180
00:09:42,938 --> 00:09:45,895
[grunts] A whole bunch
of other stuff happened.

181
00:09:45,896 --> 00:09:48,354
Ugh. Fine.
You know I'm not getting paid for this.

182
00:09:49,521 --> 00:09:52,937
[Peli] <i>So Mando tangled
with the lethal Fennec Shand,</i>

183
00:09:52,938 --> 00:09:55,353
<i>and then teamed up
with some nasty bad guys</i>

184
00:09:55,354 --> 00:09:59,520
<i>to free another nasty bad guy
from a grody prison transport.</i>

185
00:09:59,521 --> 00:10:03,853
<i>But the nasty bad guys were so nasty
that they double crossed Mando.</i>

186
00:10:03,854 --> 00:10:06,937
<i>And so he ended up putting them all
in the prison ship,</i>

187
00:10:06,938 --> 00:10:08,687
which is where I got this mug.

188
00:10:08,688 --> 00:10:09,771
[Jawas gasping]

189
00:10:10,271 --> 00:10:12,228
Come on, Mando.
It's not how it looks.

190
00:10:12,229 --> 00:10:13,979
We betrayed you for money!

191
00:10:15,104 --> 00:10:17,937
[Peli] <i>All the fighting and fleeing
was just exhausting.</i>

192
00:10:17,938 --> 00:10:20,063
<i>- Oh, can you imagine?</i>
- [honks]

193
00:10:20,604 --> 00:10:24,103
<i>So Mando was happy
when his old friend, Greef Karga,</i>

194
00:10:24,104 --> 00:10:28,770
<i>called with an offer to return to Navarro
for a truce with the bounty hunters.</i>

195
00:10:28,771 --> 00:10:31,437
<i>Mando, buddy, come on back.</i>

196
00:10:31,438 --> 00:10:33,395
<i>I swear this is not a trick.</i>

197
00:10:33,396 --> 00:10:34,478
<i>It was a trick!</i>

198
00:10:34,479 --> 00:10:37,187
He was just luring Mando
back to ambush him.

199
00:10:37,188 --> 00:10:38,645
[all booing]

200
00:10:38,646 --> 00:10:40,020
I said I'm sorry!

201
00:10:40,021 --> 00:10:42,895
I made it up to Mando
and helped them escape.

202
00:10:42,896 --> 00:10:46,770
<i>Greef organized a plan to take out
the bad guys once and for all.</i>

203
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:50,896
<i>And Kuiil helped by making sure the kid
would be protected during the battle.</i>

204
00:10:51,646 --> 00:10:54,770
You, my sensors, detect awkwardness.

205
00:10:54,771 --> 00:10:56,603
Do not fear, IG-11.

206
00:10:56,604 --> 00:10:58,062
I have spoken.

207
00:10:58,063 --> 00:11:00,353
This thing is a deadly threat.

208
00:11:00,354 --> 00:11:01,478
Not anymore.

209
00:11:01,479 --> 00:11:03,270
I have spoken again.

210
00:11:03,271 --> 00:11:06,395
Now my primary function
is to protect the child.

211
00:11:06,396 --> 00:11:09,437
He has been reprogrammed by me.

212
00:11:09,438 --> 00:11:11,770
I have spoken again.

213
00:11:11,771 --> 00:11:13,562
- Again.
- No way.

214
00:11:13,563 --> 00:11:16,103
Once a killer, always a killer.

215
00:11:16,104 --> 00:11:18,145
You do not trust my nurturing instincts.

216
00:11:18,146 --> 00:11:19,562
Initiating self-destruct.

217
00:11:19,563 --> 00:11:20,937
- Okay, okay, fine.
- [alarm blaring]

218
00:11:20,938 --> 00:11:22,187
You can watch the kid.

219
00:11:22,188 --> 00:11:24,104
Now let's go take out those Imperials.

220
00:11:26,688 --> 00:11:27,771
[both gasping]

221
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,146
[grunts]

222
00:11:30,646 --> 00:11:31,729
[grunts]

223
00:11:33,604 --> 00:11:36,313
[all screaming]

224
00:11:36,479 --> 00:11:37,770
[gasps]

225
00:11:37,771 --> 00:11:42,353
I am also experiencing
terror of the pew pew pews!

226
00:11:42,354 --> 00:11:44,438
They're gone. We win!

227
00:11:48,229 --> 00:11:50,645
They're back. We lose!

228
00:11:50,646 --> 00:11:53,229
[dramatic music playing]

229
00:11:55,729 --> 00:12:00,937
[Peli] <i>It was Moff Gideon, a super scary
former Imperial big cheese.</i>

230
00:12:00,938 --> 00:12:03,312
He was the one who wanted
the kid the whole time.

231
00:12:03,313 --> 00:12:04,313
[all booing]

232
00:12:07,271 --> 00:12:09,728
Hand over that 50-year-old child.

233
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:12,729
There's nowhere to run, Mandalorian.

234
00:12:14,063 --> 00:12:15,938
This is the Way. Down!

235
00:12:16,771 --> 00:12:18,812
- [all exclaiming]
- After them!

236
00:12:18,813 --> 00:12:22,812
I need that child... for reasons!

237
00:12:22,813 --> 00:12:25,188
[all scream]

238
00:12:26,354 --> 00:12:30,270
[Peli] <i>And they made a run for it
in the lava river under Nevarro.</i>

239
00:12:30,271 --> 00:12:32,228
Just a bit further, and we'll be safe.

240
00:12:32,229 --> 00:12:35,188
Next up, Imperial Ambush station.

241
00:12:35,646 --> 00:12:36,771
Ambush station?

242
00:12:38,313 --> 00:12:41,353
Stormtroopers.
This is gonna be a tough fight.

243
00:12:41,354 --> 00:12:44,020
[Droid] Negative.
I am programmed to protect the child.

244
00:12:44,021 --> 00:12:48,770
To fulfill my function, I will engage
the enemy alone and self-destruct.

245
00:12:48,771 --> 00:12:51,020
Thank you for your sacrifice.

246
00:12:51,021 --> 00:12:52,603
Uh, aren't you going to stop me?

247
00:12:52,604 --> 00:12:54,687
No, you're right.

248
00:12:54,688 --> 00:12:57,895
- This is the only way to save the child.
- [squeals]

249
00:12:57,896 --> 00:13:00,104
Me and my big
speech processing unit.

250
00:13:00,646 --> 00:13:05,312
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

251
00:13:05,313 --> 00:13:07,395
I am melting so slowly. Ow!

252
00:13:07,396 --> 00:13:09,145
Ow! Ow!

253
00:13:09,146 --> 00:13:11,937
Greetings, troopers,
please stand there doing nothing

254
00:13:11,938 --> 00:13:13,062
while I activate this

255
00:13:13,063 --> 00:13:14,937
- beeping thing in my chest.
- [alarm beeping]

256
00:13:14,938 --> 00:13:16,354
[stormtroopers yelling]

257
00:13:18,896 --> 00:13:22,063
[Peli] <i>It looked like they were saved,
but, uh-uh!</i>

258
00:13:23,979 --> 00:13:25,146
[laughs wickedly]

259
00:13:25,646 --> 00:13:26,729
Moff Gideon!

260
00:13:28,813 --> 00:13:30,896
[gunfire]

261
00:13:39,104 --> 00:13:42,063
[laughs wickedly]

262
00:13:44,021 --> 00:13:46,520
You can't touch me in here, Mando!

263
00:13:46,521 --> 00:13:49,812
[laughs wickedly]

264
00:13:49,813 --> 00:13:52,187
- Uh-oh!
- [beeping]

265
00:13:52,188 --> 00:13:55,395
I told the Empire to put
windshield wipers on these things.

266
00:13:55,396 --> 00:13:56,604
[explosion]

267
00:14:00,563 --> 00:14:02,728
Uh, do you think we should go make sure

268
00:14:02,729 --> 00:14:06,271
Moff Gideon didn't somehow
survive that crash?

269
00:14:07,146 --> 00:14:08,229
[both] Nah.

270
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:17,145
I will get that child yet.

271
00:14:17,146 --> 00:14:18,812
- [phone beeping]
- [line ringing]

272
00:14:18,813 --> 00:14:21,229
Mom, can you come pick me up?

273
00:14:22,979 --> 00:14:27,812
That was a noble sacrifice
IG-11 made to save the child,

274
00:14:27,813 --> 00:14:32,103
- blowing himself to pieces like that.
- I did what I had to do.

275
00:14:32,104 --> 00:14:33,187
[exclaims]

276
00:14:33,188 --> 00:14:35,312
How are you here?
You self-destructed!

277
00:14:35,313 --> 00:14:37,645
I got better, then I got destroyed again.

278
00:14:37,646 --> 00:14:40,020
Then I got better again.
It's sort of what I do.

279
00:14:40,021 --> 00:14:41,103
- [distant explosion]
- [all exclaim]

280
00:14:41,104 --> 00:14:42,104
What was that?

281
00:14:44,438 --> 00:14:45,771
- Imperials!
- [gun cocking]

282
00:14:54,854 --> 00:14:55,854
[guns cocking]

283
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:59,437
Wow, it stinks to be those guys.

284
00:14:59,438 --> 00:15:00,770
Is this where the party's at?

285
00:15:00,771 --> 00:15:02,187
- Migs?
- Mando!

286
00:15:02,188 --> 00:15:04,687
- Happy birthday!
- It's not my birthday.

287
00:15:04,688 --> 00:15:06,562
Oh, that's good.
I didn't get you anything.

288
00:15:06,563 --> 00:15:10,478
Do you like my ride? I stole it
from a pirate junkyard on Jakku.

289
00:15:10,479 --> 00:15:13,312
Wait. Why would you do anything nice
for Mando?

290
00:15:13,313 --> 00:15:14,520
He put you in prison.

291
00:15:14,521 --> 00:15:15,937
He's my buddy now.

292
00:15:15,938 --> 00:15:19,312
He busted me out to help him rescue
the kid after the Imperials kidnapped him.

293
00:15:19,313 --> 00:15:20,853
[stutters] Kidnapped?

294
00:15:20,854 --> 00:15:23,020
Oh! It's a wicked great story.

295
00:15:23,021 --> 00:15:25,062
And I was there for at least 20% of it.

296
00:15:25,063 --> 00:15:27,312
So Mando wasn't alone anymore.

297
00:15:27,313 --> 00:15:29,687
He had a kid, but now he had to bring him

298
00:15:29,688 --> 00:15:31,228
to be with his own kind,

299
00:15:31,229 --> 00:15:35,395
the powerful guardians of justice
in the galaxy, the Jethros.

300
00:15:35,396 --> 00:15:37,437
- [all] Jedi!
- Right.

301
00:15:37,438 --> 00:15:39,728
- Jedis.
- Jedi!

302
00:15:39,729 --> 00:15:42,353
Okay, Jedi, get over yourself.

303
00:15:42,354 --> 00:15:44,103
Yourselves!

304
00:15:44,104 --> 00:15:45,478
All right?

305
00:15:45,479 --> 00:15:48,645
So, anyway, Mando heard
there was another Mandalorian

306
00:15:48,646 --> 00:15:51,520
<i>and Mos Pelgo,
who could help him find some Jedi.</i>

307
00:15:51,521 --> 00:15:55,520
<i>But when he got there, it wasn't
a Mandalorian, it was just a regular guy.</i>

308
00:15:55,521 --> 00:15:57,687
<i>A rugged marshal named Cobb Salad.</i>

309
00:15:57,688 --> 00:16:01,103
Vanth. The name is Cobb Vanth.

310
00:16:01,104 --> 00:16:02,728
<i>Okay, fine!</i>

311
00:16:02,729 --> 00:16:04,853
- Cobb Vanth.
- Thank you.

312
00:16:04,854 --> 00:16:07,562
He was wearing some other guy's armor.

313
00:16:07,563 --> 00:16:09,603
Oh! You'll never guess whose armor it was.

314
00:16:09,604 --> 00:16:11,603
It's a big name. Very famous.

315
00:16:11,604 --> 00:16:13,478
So spoil it!

316
00:16:13,479 --> 00:16:17,103
Mando believed the armor
should only be worn by a Mandalorian.

317
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:19,312
So the marshal proposed a deal.

318
00:16:19,313 --> 00:16:21,270
I'll tell you what. You can have the armor

319
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:24,645
if you help me and my people
here with a problem.

320
00:16:24,646 --> 00:16:26,937
[sighs in exasperation] Let me guess.

321
00:16:26,938 --> 00:16:29,020
I have to fight a monster.

322
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:31,395
No, you don't have to fight a monster.

323
00:16:31,396 --> 00:16:33,271
You have to fight a dragon.

324
00:16:34,646 --> 00:16:36,853
[roaring]

325
00:16:36,854 --> 00:16:38,812
- [whimpers]
- Here we go again.

326
00:16:38,813 --> 00:16:41,645
I need you to loan me
a bantha strapped with explosives.

327
00:16:41,646 --> 00:16:45,228
Well, you're in luck, because I always
keep a couple of those lying around.

328
00:16:45,229 --> 00:16:47,020
[grunts]

329
00:16:47,021 --> 00:16:48,770
[roaring]

330
00:16:48,771 --> 00:16:51,854
- [bell dinging]
- Dragon, come to dinner!

331
00:16:59,313 --> 00:17:01,853
[Mando] This is going to stink.

332
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:04,063
- [roaring]
- [gasps]

333
00:17:06,354 --> 00:17:07,812
[belches]

334
00:17:07,813 --> 00:17:09,104
[beeps]

335
00:17:13,771 --> 00:17:15,520
[Migs] Mando saved the day.

336
00:17:15,521 --> 00:17:19,187
<i>And if he blew up two more monsters,
he'd get a free sandwich.</i>

337
00:17:19,188 --> 00:17:23,520
{\an8}Try the roast womp rat on rye.
It's to die for.

338
00:17:23,521 --> 00:17:25,062
[Migs] <i>Mando left with the armor</i>

339
00:17:25,063 --> 00:17:28,270
<i>and a lead on where to find some Jedi
to help the kid.</i>

340
00:17:28,271 --> 00:17:32,228
And you won't believe
all the crazy stuff that happened next.

341
00:17:32,229 --> 00:17:35,562
This is the 80% part that I wasn't
there for, but here we go anyway.

342
00:17:35,563 --> 00:17:38,520
<i>First, he had to take this frog lady
to meet a frog husband.</i>

343
00:17:38,521 --> 00:17:39,978
<i>But they had a crash landing.</i>

344
00:17:39,979 --> 00:17:43,145
<i>And Mando had to fight off
another giant monster.</i>

345
00:17:43,146 --> 00:17:45,187
<i>This time, a big spider.</i>

346
00:17:45,188 --> 00:17:49,520
<i>The frog husband sent Mando
to meet this lady Mando named Bo-Katan.</i>

347
00:17:49,521 --> 00:17:52,687
<i>They got in a crazy battle,
and then Bo-Katan told them...</i>

348
00:17:52,688 --> 00:17:55,770
I gotta get that dark saber thing
from Moff Bad Guy

349
00:17:55,771 --> 00:17:57,978
and reclaim the throne of Mandalore.

350
00:17:57,979 --> 00:18:00,228
Good luck with that, but I'm outie.

351
00:18:00,229 --> 00:18:04,187
[Migs] <i>So Mando and the kid went back
to Nevarro and fought off pirates.</i>

352
00:18:04,188 --> 00:18:05,271
[grunts]

353
00:18:06,646 --> 00:18:09,895
[Migs] <i>Then they found
the great Jedi, Ahsoka Tano.</i>

354
00:18:09,896 --> 00:18:11,103
<i>And she was all like...</i>

355
00:18:11,104 --> 00:18:12,687
Pretty snazzy entrance, huh?

356
00:18:12,688 --> 00:18:15,687
Ever see anybody spin
two of these light up dealies?

357
00:18:15,688 --> 00:18:18,812
[Migs] <i>Mando and Ahsoka teamed up
to defeat an evil tyrant</i>

358
00:18:18,813 --> 00:18:20,603
<i>and free a whole town.</i>

359
00:18:20,604 --> 00:18:24,312
<i>Ahsoka sent Mando to a planet where
the kid could reach out to the other Jedi.</i>

360
00:18:24,313 --> 00:18:26,020
<i>But what they didn't know was</i>

361
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:28,312
<i>Moff Bad Guy put a tracking beacon
on Mando's ship.</i>

362
00:18:28,313 --> 00:18:29,395
- [chuckles]
- [alarm blaring]

363
00:18:29,396 --> 00:18:31,937
<i>So Moff Bad Guy
was on his way to take the kid</i>

364
00:18:31,938 --> 00:18:34,353
<i>who Mando finally found out
his name!</i>

365
00:18:34,354 --> 00:18:37,312
He is called Goo-Goo.

366
00:18:37,313 --> 00:18:40,145
Grogu. His name is Grogu.

367
00:18:40,146 --> 00:18:41,688
At least I didn't call him Baby Yoda!

368
00:18:42,521 --> 00:18:46,520
So Mando got the kid to the Jedi place
where he could connect to the Jedi

369
00:18:46,521 --> 00:18:49,437
<i>using that Jedi mind thing
that all the Jedi do.</i>

370
00:18:49,438 --> 00:18:51,354
Are you happy now that I got it right?

371
00:18:53,646 --> 00:18:56,312
- [Mando] Is that a Jedi?
- [Migs] <i>It wasn't a Jedi.</i>

372
00:18:56,313 --> 00:18:58,020
<i>It was a mystery adversary.</i>

373
00:18:58,021 --> 00:19:04,103
<i>Another bounty hunter, the very same one
whose armor Cob Vanth gave to Mando,</i>

374
00:19:04,104 --> 00:19:07,312
<i>probably the most famous
bounty hunter of all!</i>

375
00:19:07,313 --> 00:19:10,687
- [whooping]
- Go ahead. You tell it. It

376
00:19:10,688 --> 00:19:14,313
It was Boba Fett
and he was with Fennec Shand.

377
00:19:16,521 --> 00:19:18,103
[Mando] Hey, that's my armor!

378
00:19:18,104 --> 00:19:20,270
I fought off a big monster to get it.

379
00:19:20,271 --> 00:19:22,937
I lost it in the stomach
of a bigger monster!

380
00:19:22,938 --> 00:19:24,062
[Peli] Uh, guys.

381
00:19:24,063 --> 00:19:26,603
guys, I have a better ship.

382
00:19:26,604 --> 00:19:28,312
My ship is way better.

383
00:19:28,313 --> 00:19:30,978
You can't even tell which part
is the front and which is the back.

384
00:19:30,979 --> 00:19:32,562
That's what's so great about it.

385
00:19:32,563 --> 00:19:37,854
Hey! Why don't you two stop
your ship measuring contest and look up!

386
00:19:41,188 --> 00:19:42,520
They blew up my ship.

387
00:19:42,521 --> 00:19:43,812
He left mine alone.

388
00:19:43,813 --> 00:19:45,187
They know how great it is.

389
00:19:45,188 --> 00:19:47,187
Enough about the ships!

390
00:19:47,188 --> 00:19:48,395
The kid is in trouble.

391
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:50,271
[dramatic music playing]

392
00:19:52,229 --> 00:19:53,313
Yoink!

393
00:19:54,854 --> 00:19:56,188
Grogu!

394
00:20:00,313 --> 00:20:01,396
[whistles]

395
00:20:02,938 --> 00:20:05,770
How do you like me now, Mando?

396
00:20:05,771 --> 00:20:09,687
I didn't like you before,
and now I like you even less.

397
00:20:09,688 --> 00:20:11,937
That makes sense!

398
00:20:11,938 --> 00:20:13,188
Bye.

399
00:20:14,313 --> 00:20:15,645
[Migs] <i>Mando was devastated.</i>

400
00:20:15,646 --> 00:20:18,478
He knew he had to save Grogu
from those evil imps.

401
00:20:18,479 --> 00:20:20,812
But now he had a group
of friends to help him.

402
00:20:20,813 --> 00:20:23,062
And that's pretty good where I come from.

403
00:20:23,063 --> 00:20:25,270
Huh. Where do you come from?

404
00:20:25,271 --> 00:20:27,104
Where else? South Bespin!

405
00:20:33,938 --> 00:20:37,812
Your special blood
is going to make me invincible.

406
00:20:37,813 --> 00:20:40,312
Those are my reasons.

407
00:20:40,313 --> 00:20:41,603
[whimpers]

408
00:20:41,604 --> 00:20:44,062
Yes. Accept your fate.

409
00:20:44,063 --> 00:20:45,395
It is your destiny.

410
00:20:45,396 --> 00:20:48,437
- [whimpering]
- You don't have to overdo it.

411
00:20:48,438 --> 00:20:49,603
[grunting]

412
00:20:49,604 --> 00:20:50,771
Why are you--

413
00:20:53,771 --> 00:20:55,937
[beeping]

414
00:20:55,938 --> 00:20:57,313
[screams, grunts]

415
00:20:57,896 --> 00:20:58,978
[groans]

416
00:20:58,979 --> 00:21:00,228
[Migs] <i>It was on.</i>

417
00:21:00,229 --> 00:21:04,228
<i>Mando battled his way onto the ship
with the help of Bo-Katan.</i>

418
00:21:04,229 --> 00:21:06,187
- It was awesome.
- [both grunting]

419
00:21:06,188 --> 00:21:07,728
I got you now.

420
00:21:07,729 --> 00:21:09,228
- [laughs wickedly]
- [grunts]

421
00:21:09,229 --> 00:21:11,104
[yells]

422
00:21:17,188 --> 00:21:18,271
[Mando] Come on.

423
00:21:18,438 --> 00:21:20,438
- [guns cocking]
- [elevator dings]

424
00:21:24,604 --> 00:21:26,479
- [swishing]
- [gunfire]

425
00:21:29,271 --> 00:21:30,771
[R2-D2 beeping]

426
00:21:34,646 --> 00:21:38,938
[Migs] <i>The battle ended with the arrival
of the most famous Jedi of them all.</i>

427
00:21:41,313 --> 00:21:44,520
It looks like you were expecting us
to know who you are.

428
00:21:44,521 --> 00:21:46,813
I'm Luke Skywalker.

429
00:21:48,646 --> 00:21:50,938
My father was Darth Vader?

430
00:21:52,521 --> 00:21:55,187
Oh, come on! I'm kind of a big deal!

431
00:21:55,188 --> 00:21:58,062
[Mando] Mm. If you say so.

432
00:21:58,063 --> 00:22:01,478
[sighs] I was beckoned by the call
of a young one named Grogu.

433
00:22:01,479 --> 00:22:03,562
- Where is he?
- At your feet.

434
00:22:03,563 --> 00:22:04,853
[speaking indistinctly]

435
00:22:04,854 --> 00:22:06,187
You're not very big.

436
00:22:06,188 --> 00:22:07,812
- [groans]
- Ugh!

437
00:22:07,813 --> 00:22:10,187
Right, right. Size matters not.

438
00:22:10,188 --> 00:22:13,145
He needs to be trained. By a Jedi.

439
00:22:13,146 --> 00:22:16,938
I know.
Can I have a moment with him?

440
00:22:18,813 --> 00:22:20,103
Kid.

441
00:22:20,104 --> 00:22:22,603
I guess this is goodbye.

442
00:22:22,604 --> 00:22:26,021
I have to let you see
my face this one time.

443
00:22:31,854 --> 00:22:33,353
Goodbye, Grogu.

444
00:22:33,354 --> 00:22:39,438
I hope I see you again,
maybe in a whole other series of events.

445
00:22:49,729 --> 00:22:52,020
[Migs] <i>And so the kid left with that
Luke guy</i>

446
00:22:52,021 --> 00:22:54,437
<i>and his little beepee-boopy friend.</i>

447
00:22:54,438 --> 00:22:58,353
Grogu had finally found his family,
but Mando had lost his.

448
00:22:58,354 --> 00:23:00,604
[all sobbing]

449
00:23:01,604 --> 00:23:03,520
Don't worry, it all worked out.

450
00:23:03,521 --> 00:23:04,937
He's here, isn't he?

451
00:23:04,938 --> 00:23:07,979
[all cheering]

452
00:23:10,021 --> 00:23:13,937
We tracked that thieving Migs
and the ship he stole from us

453
00:23:13,938 --> 00:23:16,853
to the Mos Eisley Cantina
on Tatooine.

454
00:23:16,854 --> 00:23:21,478
But get this, he's at a party
with The Mandalorian

455
00:23:21,479 --> 00:23:24,062
<i>and that little green kid!</i>

456
00:23:24,063 --> 00:23:25,770
Our archenemies!

457
00:23:25,771 --> 00:23:27,603
Well, The Mandalorian

458
00:23:27,604 --> 00:23:32,728
may have wiped us out of Nevarro,
but today, we pirates will triumph!

459
00:23:32,729 --> 00:23:34,312
[all cheering]

460
00:23:34,313 --> 00:23:37,270
<i>You go out and collect
every pirate in the sector,</i>

461
00:23:37,271 --> 00:23:41,728
<i>and when you have them all together,
launch an attack on that cantina!</i>

462
00:23:41,729 --> 00:23:43,812
[laughs wickedly]

463
00:23:43,813 --> 00:23:47,813
<i>We shall leave our enemies reeling!</i>

464
00:23:48,021 --> 00:23:52,478
- [upbeat music playing]
- [indistinct chatter]

465
00:23:52,479 --> 00:23:53,563
[squealing]

466
00:23:54,604 --> 00:23:56,603
[whimpering]

467
00:23:56,604 --> 00:23:58,978
Hey, take it easy
with the little guy.

468
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,187
Okay, that's it.

469
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:02,478
This party is a bit too off the hook.

470
00:24:02,479 --> 00:24:05,978
- Ah, yeah!
- The kid and I should be heading home.

471
00:24:05,979 --> 00:24:08,937
- [all groaning]
- You can't leave now.

472
00:24:08,938 --> 00:24:10,770
All the guests haven't arrived.

473
00:24:10,771 --> 00:24:13,270
You have so many friends who want
to see you.

474
00:24:13,271 --> 00:24:14,895
That sounds exhausting.

475
00:24:14,896 --> 00:24:17,062
You're gonna make me cry
and you know I don't cry.

476
00:24:17,063 --> 00:24:18,603
- [Grogu whines]
- [groans]

477
00:24:18,604 --> 00:24:21,270
You see this sad face? It can get sadder.

478
00:24:21,271 --> 00:24:22,729
We really have to go.

479
00:24:23,354 --> 00:24:24,895
[somber instrumental music playing]

480
00:24:24,896 --> 00:24:27,270
Okay, fine! We'll stay.

481
00:24:27,271 --> 00:24:28,687
[all cheering]

482
00:24:28,688 --> 00:24:30,520
The story continues.

483
00:24:30,521 --> 00:24:33,520
Oh! Oh! Mando, tell us what happened
after Grogu left with Luke Skywalker.

484
00:24:33,521 --> 00:24:37,270
And what did Boba Fett do
after he fought the Imperials with you?

485
00:24:37,271 --> 00:24:40,312
That's his story,
and he's not here to tell it.

486
00:24:40,313 --> 00:24:44,937
Even if he was, Boba Fett is not one
to trumpet his own accomplishments.

487
00:24:44,938 --> 00:24:46,353
[trumpets playing]

488
00:24:46,354 --> 00:24:49,187
Felicitations upon this festive gathering!

489
00:24:49,188 --> 00:24:53,562
presenting the most excellent
Daimyo of Tatooine,

490
00:24:53,563 --> 00:24:55,812
the sort of son of Jango Fett.

491
00:24:55,813 --> 00:24:57,937
Boba Fett!

492
00:24:57,938 --> 00:25:01,312
And his guests Fennec Shand
and Krrsantan!

493
00:25:01,313 --> 00:25:03,562
[trumpets]

494
00:25:03,563 --> 00:25:05,853
Just ignore me. I'm not here.

495
00:25:05,854 --> 00:25:08,270
A little over the top, don't you think?

496
00:25:08,271 --> 00:25:11,562
When you spend months
eating dirt in the desert

497
00:25:11,563 --> 00:25:15,145
you can tell me how to live
when things start to go good.

498
00:25:15,146 --> 00:25:18,937
[gasps] You're Boba Fett,
the greatest bounty hunter of them all.

499
00:25:18,938 --> 00:25:20,520
He's okay.

500
00:25:20,521 --> 00:25:24,353
[stutters] Tell us how you got to be
Daimyo on Tatooine.

501
00:25:24,354 --> 00:25:27,353
No, no. I want to know how Mando
got Grogu back.

502
00:25:27,354 --> 00:25:29,603
Well, I want to hear about Boba Fett.

503
00:25:29,604 --> 00:25:30,812
Good sirs!

504
00:25:30,813 --> 00:25:35,562
The two stories you wish to hear
are serendipitously intertwined,

505
00:25:35,563 --> 00:25:40,103
and both end with the victory
of the heroic Boba Fett.

506
00:25:40,104 --> 00:25:43,937
Gather round and I shall delight you
with this glorious tale.

507
00:25:43,938 --> 00:25:46,603
It's a whole actual book?

508
00:25:46,604 --> 00:25:48,020
Not a big reader, huh?

509
00:25:48,021 --> 00:25:51,937
I have to get up early in the morning,
skip a few chapters.

510
00:25:51,938 --> 00:25:54,312
- I live to serve.
- [Grogu coos]

511
00:25:54,313 --> 00:25:57,395
Boba Fett and Fennec Shand
returned to Tatooine,

512
00:25:57,396 --> 00:26:01,353
<i>where Boba Fett took care
of some unfinished business</i>

513
00:26:01,354 --> 00:26:04,771
<i>at the domicile of his former employer.</i>

514
00:26:06,771 --> 00:26:08,645
[speaking Huttese] <i>Die wonna wonga.</i>

515
00:26:08,646 --> 00:26:09,770
[guns cocking]

516
00:26:09,771 --> 00:26:12,021
<i>No wanna wonga!</i>

517
00:26:13,479 --> 00:26:17,103
[majordomo in English] <i>While Boba Fett
settled into his new Daimyo-citude,</i>

518
00:26:17,104 --> 00:26:19,645
<i>The Mandalorian
was on a quest of his own.</i>

519
00:26:19,646 --> 00:26:22,478
<i>Sadly, the razor crest was no more.</i>

520
00:26:22,479 --> 00:26:25,520
<i>So he visited Peli Motto
to acquire a new vehicle.</i>

521
00:26:25,521 --> 00:26:29,353
I want to go see the kid,
just to make sure he's safe.

522
00:26:29,354 --> 00:26:30,478
Oh, you're so cute.

523
00:26:30,479 --> 00:26:34,520
Admit it. You love the little guy
and you miss him. We won't tease you.

524
00:26:34,521 --> 00:26:37,728
Fine! Yes, I... I miss him.

525
00:26:37,729 --> 00:26:40,104
[all giggling]

526
00:26:41,229 --> 00:26:44,728
When I see Grogu,
I'm going to give him this.

527
00:26:44,729 --> 00:26:46,603
Very, very funny. That's funny.

528
00:26:46,604 --> 00:26:47,728
What's the real gift?

529
00:26:47,729 --> 00:26:51,520
That's it. It's a suit of chain mail
made from Beskar steel.

530
00:26:51,521 --> 00:26:54,020
Right. Right, right.
You know, kids hate clothes.

531
00:26:54,021 --> 00:26:58,562
They want a nice speeder bike or something
with tassels on the handlebars.

532
00:26:58,563 --> 00:27:00,770
Something like that.
You know, something that moves.

533
00:27:00,771 --> 00:27:03,478
Beskar is sacred to all Mandalorians!

534
00:27:03,479 --> 00:27:05,478
Ugh, fine! You do you.

535
00:27:05,479 --> 00:27:06,770
I'll help you go see the kid.

536
00:27:06,771 --> 00:27:08,228
I got a new ship for you.

537
00:27:08,229 --> 00:27:12,478
I hope you're wearing socks
because they're about to get knocked off!

538
00:27:12,479 --> 00:27:14,770
Ta-da! Isn't it great?

539
00:27:14,771 --> 00:27:16,020
Uh...

540
00:27:16,021 --> 00:27:18,978
Only used once
by a 10-year-old on Boonta Eve.

541
00:27:18,979 --> 00:27:20,771
Nice kid. Really hated sand.

542
00:27:21,438 --> 00:27:22,520
No.

543
00:27:22,521 --> 00:27:24,145
Right, right, right, right, right.
Not for you, not for you.

544
00:27:24,146 --> 00:27:26,603
I got it, I got it, I got it, I got it.
How about this?

545
00:27:26,604 --> 00:27:27,770
Hard pass.

546
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:30,395
Picky, picky, picky.
There's plenty more to choose from.

547
00:27:30,396 --> 00:27:31,937
Nope. Uh-huh.

548
00:27:31,938 --> 00:27:33,563
Wow. No!

549
00:27:33,688 --> 00:27:36,603
- [beeping]
- [Mando] No way! Never.

550
00:27:36,604 --> 00:27:38,812
You are a tough customer.

551
00:27:38,813 --> 00:27:42,395
All right. I was saving this
last one for you. Russell!

552
00:27:42,396 --> 00:27:43,604
Hit it.

553
00:27:44,271 --> 00:27:47,062
It's a Naboo N-1 Starfighter.

554
00:27:47,063 --> 00:27:50,062
This beauty was used
by the Royal Security Force

555
00:27:50,063 --> 00:27:54,145
during the Clone Wars,
and it's got the battle scars to prove it.

556
00:27:54,146 --> 00:27:56,770
And because you hate droids
and I like you,

557
00:27:56,771 --> 00:28:00,270
I've replaced the Astromech slot
with a seat for that

558
00:28:00,271 --> 00:28:02,478
special little green-eared
someone in your life.

559
00:28:02,479 --> 00:28:05,270
Total retail price?
You couldn't afford it.

560
00:28:05,271 --> 00:28:09,187
My asking price?
Give that kid a big hug for me.

561
00:28:09,188 --> 00:28:10,395
Sold.

562
00:28:10,396 --> 00:28:12,188
- [keys jingling]
- [whistles]

563
00:28:13,688 --> 00:28:19,228
So The Mandalorian flew off to pay
a visit to his diminutive green ward.

564
00:28:19,229 --> 00:28:23,978
This proved to be a case
of easier said than done.

565
00:28:23,979 --> 00:28:25,687
Grogu, it's me!

566
00:28:25,688 --> 00:28:27,395
- Daddy!
- No!

567
00:28:27,396 --> 00:28:29,020
You cannot see him.

568
00:28:29,021 --> 00:28:30,937
He is my responsibility.

569
00:28:30,938 --> 00:28:32,478
- [grunts]
- [electricity crackling]

570
00:28:32,479 --> 00:28:33,562
[beeping]

571
00:28:33,563 --> 00:28:36,187
Okay! Take it easy, big guy.

572
00:28:36,188 --> 00:28:37,188
[beeping]

573
00:28:39,188 --> 00:28:43,937
I know you miss Grogu, and I sympathize,
but he is with Master Luke.

574
00:28:43,938 --> 00:28:47,395
We can't let Grogu's attachment
to you disrupt his training.

575
00:28:47,396 --> 00:28:49,437
Use the Force, Grogu.

576
00:28:49,438 --> 00:28:51,271
Pick up a rock.

577
00:28:53,479 --> 00:28:55,896
- Good.
- Ah! [chuckles]

578
00:28:59,688 --> 00:29:00,854
Very good!

579
00:29:02,104 --> 00:29:03,812
Stupid good.

580
00:29:03,813 --> 00:29:06,770
Wow. You're force building
at a high school level.

581
00:29:06,771 --> 00:29:09,104
[laughs] Ooh!

582
00:29:10,396 --> 00:29:12,646
- [coos]
- [grunts]

583
00:29:13,729 --> 00:29:16,395
We'll try again after lunch. [grunts]

584
00:29:16,396 --> 00:29:18,603
I don't want the kid to flunk.

585
00:29:18,604 --> 00:29:22,313
Eventually, Grogu
will have to choose his own path.

586
00:29:23,313 --> 00:29:25,770
- But for now...
- I'll go.

587
00:29:25,771 --> 00:29:27,771
But can you give him this?

588
00:29:28,146 --> 00:29:30,687
- [beeping]
- Yes, that's it.

589
00:29:30,688 --> 00:29:32,520
- That's the gift.
- [beeping]

590
00:29:32,521 --> 00:29:34,395
No, it's not a speeder bike.

591
00:29:34,396 --> 00:29:36,812
- It's precious Beskar steel!
- [grunts]

592
00:29:36,813 --> 00:29:39,187
No, he can't sell the steel
to buy a speeder bike.

593
00:29:39,188 --> 00:29:43,228
<i>So The Mandalorian returned
to Tatooine to assist Boba Fett,</i>

594
00:29:43,229 --> 00:29:46,687
<i>who is encountering fierce resistance
to his rule</i>

595
00:29:46,688 --> 00:29:50,062
<i>from the dreaded Pyke crime syndicate.</i>

596
00:29:50,063 --> 00:29:55,062
<i>The Mandalorian was a warrior,
and now he was back in his element.</i>

597
00:29:55,063 --> 00:29:58,270
I, regrettably, was not in my element.

598
00:29:58,271 --> 00:30:04,353
<i>While Mando, Fennec and their allies
waged a valiant fight, Boba Fett...</i>

599
00:30:04,354 --> 00:30:05,812
<i>ran away.</i>

600
00:30:05,813 --> 00:30:08,020
I went to get help! Tell it right!

601
00:30:08,021 --> 00:30:09,937
Yes, great and merciful one.

602
00:30:09,938 --> 00:30:13,770
Boba Fett heroically ran away to get help.

603
00:30:13,771 --> 00:30:16,812
<i>Meanwhile, Luke Skywalker presented Grogu</i>

604
00:30:16,813 --> 00:30:19,770
<i>with the gift
The Mandalorian left behind.</i>

605
00:30:19,771 --> 00:30:20,895
[speaking indistinctly]

606
00:30:20,896 --> 00:30:24,937
The Force is strong with Grogu
but he cannot be distracted like this.

607
00:30:24,938 --> 00:30:27,437
He has to choose between his training
with me

608
00:30:27,438 --> 00:30:29,520
and reuniting with The Mandalorian.

609
00:30:29,521 --> 00:30:33,270
I think he's already made his choice.

610
00:30:33,271 --> 00:30:36,020
[laughing]

611
00:30:36,021 --> 00:30:38,103
Yes. Yes, it's very you.

612
00:30:38,104 --> 00:30:39,395
Oh! [giggles]

613
00:30:39,396 --> 00:30:43,687
[sighs] I sure hope my next student
won't be this difficult.

614
00:30:43,688 --> 00:30:45,687
[dramatic music playing]

615
00:30:45,688 --> 00:30:47,229
[grunts]

616
00:30:48,021 --> 00:30:52,062
<i>Things were looking bad
for The Mandalorian</i>

617
00:30:52,063 --> 00:30:56,937
<i>but then Boba Fett made
his triumphant, heroic return,</i>

618
00:30:56,938 --> 00:30:59,312
because he didn't really run away.

619
00:30:59,313 --> 00:31:01,603
He was always there.

620
00:31:01,604 --> 00:31:03,353
Now you're overdoing it.

621
00:31:03,354 --> 00:31:06,479
[dramatic music playing]

622
00:31:08,021 --> 00:31:10,853
Finally! A monster I can like!

623
00:31:10,854 --> 00:31:14,145
[yelps] I take that back!

624
00:31:14,146 --> 00:31:16,604
[grunting]

625
00:31:17,854 --> 00:31:20,228
Mando, stop playing with that rancor!

626
00:31:20,229 --> 00:31:22,437
[straining] It's playing with me!

627
00:31:22,438 --> 00:31:24,562
Good thing I brought somebody with me.

628
00:31:24,563 --> 00:31:25,645
[giggles]

629
00:31:25,646 --> 00:31:27,562
Kid! [grunting]

630
00:31:27,563 --> 00:31:30,978
- Am I happy... to see... you.
- [thudding]

631
00:31:30,979 --> 00:31:32,520
Use the Force!

632
00:31:32,521 --> 00:31:34,938
Knock this monster into the next galaxy.

633
00:31:36,813 --> 00:31:39,063
[growling]

634
00:31:41,438 --> 00:31:43,812
- [Grogu grunts]
- [Mando sighs]

635
00:31:43,813 --> 00:31:45,687
Putting it to sleep works, too.

636
00:31:45,688 --> 00:31:48,937
And so, with the help of the returning
Din Djarin,

637
00:31:48,938 --> 00:31:51,770
the great Daimyo Boba Fett

638
00:31:51,771 --> 00:31:55,645
defeated the Pykes
and brought peace to Mos Espa.

639
00:31:55,646 --> 00:32:01,062
For all of our firepower, in the end,
it was the little one who saved us.

640
00:32:01,063 --> 00:32:02,603
What? What about me?

641
00:32:02,604 --> 00:32:05,728
I brought him there from the spaceport.
I was his ride!

642
00:32:05,729 --> 00:32:07,645
Yes, congratulations.

643
00:32:07,646 --> 00:32:12,645
Things looked good for Mando and Grogu
but there was danger ahead.

644
00:32:12,646 --> 00:32:14,645
For unbeknownst to them,

645
00:32:14,646 --> 00:32:18,020
Moff Gideon had escaped
New Republic custody

646
00:32:18,021 --> 00:32:19,895
- and was closing--
- [all exclaiming]

647
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:21,895
- [thudding]
- [all screaming]

648
00:32:21,896 --> 00:32:23,687
[yelling]

649
00:32:23,688 --> 00:32:26,937
- Hello, Mando.
- [guns cocking]

650
00:32:26,938 --> 00:32:30,020
Happy birthday to us.

651
00:32:30,021 --> 00:32:33,103
It's not my birthday,
it's just a party!

652
00:32:33,104 --> 00:32:34,520
[Mando] Pirates.

653
00:32:34,521 --> 00:32:36,812
We won't be able
to hold them off on our own.

654
00:32:36,813 --> 00:32:42,313
I shall engage them diplomatically
and negotiate an amicable settlement.

655
00:32:42,813 --> 00:32:44,520
[lasers firing]

656
00:32:44,521 --> 00:32:47,978
Not so amicable. [whimpers]

657
00:32:47,979 --> 00:32:49,312
Nobody panic.

658
00:32:49,313 --> 00:32:52,395
Bo-Katan and her fellow Mandalorians
will be here soon,

659
00:32:52,396 --> 00:32:54,437
and they will help us. I know it.

660
00:32:54,438 --> 00:32:56,603
How can you be so sure?

661
00:32:56,604 --> 00:32:58,770
Because we defeated Moff Gideon together.

662
00:32:58,771 --> 00:33:02,187
Because we are heirs to a legacy
of commitment and devotion

663
00:33:02,188 --> 00:33:05,353
going back to the ancient
ancestors of Mandalore.

664
00:33:05,354 --> 00:33:07,978
And also because she's
sitting right over there.

665
00:33:07,979 --> 00:33:09,271
[grunts]

666
00:33:09,646 --> 00:33:11,895
No way I'd ever miss your party.

667
00:33:11,896 --> 00:33:13,645
Thanks for the invite, Peli.

668
00:33:13,646 --> 00:33:14,646
- [thudding]
- [all exclaiming]

669
00:33:18,354 --> 00:33:22,103
No more inspirational speeches, Mando.

670
00:33:22,104 --> 00:33:23,437
Give up.

671
00:33:23,438 --> 00:33:25,812
You'll have to come through all of us.

672
00:33:25,813 --> 00:33:28,771
But these guys first.
Got to adjust the hair for the helmet.

673
00:33:31,063 --> 00:33:33,604
- [all grunting]
- [guns firing]

674
00:33:34,604 --> 00:33:35,937
No! No, no, no.

675
00:33:35,938 --> 00:33:38,520
[exclaiming]

676
00:33:38,521 --> 00:33:41,354
[all exclaiming]

677
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:43,729
[screaming]

678
00:33:45,021 --> 00:33:47,063
Gonna need some help here.

679
00:33:48,688 --> 00:33:50,937
[all cheering]

680
00:33:50,938 --> 00:33:54,312
Wow! Boba Fett, you're the best.

681
00:33:54,313 --> 00:33:56,228
Hey, what are we? Bantha Poodoo?

682
00:33:56,229 --> 00:33:57,937
Welcome to my world.

683
00:33:57,938 --> 00:33:59,062
We're not safe yet.

684
00:33:59,063 --> 00:34:02,312
Those pirates will be back
with plenty of reinforcements.

685
00:34:02,313 --> 00:34:03,978
We're going to be all right.

686
00:34:03,979 --> 00:34:07,103
Just like in our final victory
over Moff Gideon on Mandalore.

687
00:34:07,104 --> 00:34:08,478
What did you do there?

688
00:34:08,479 --> 00:34:11,478
It's a good story. I will tell you.

689
00:34:11,479 --> 00:34:14,228
Does everybody have to tell a story?

690
00:34:14,229 --> 00:34:17,479
Yes! It's very inspiring.

691
00:34:18,604 --> 00:34:20,562
[sighs wearily] I'm sure it is.

692
00:34:20,563 --> 00:34:22,063
Go right ahead.

693
00:34:23,438 --> 00:34:26,437
Din Djarin had finally
reunited with Grogu.

694
00:34:26,438 --> 00:34:30,645
Now he needed to redeem himself
and reclaim his status as a Mandalorian.

695
00:34:30,646 --> 00:34:34,395
<i>So he and Grogu journeyed to be
with the armorer and her covert.</i>

696
00:34:34,396 --> 00:34:38,895
Din Djarin, you have proven
your valor in many battles,

697
00:34:38,896 --> 00:34:41,770
saved the Mandalorians from great harm,

698
00:34:41,771 --> 00:34:45,604
- and defeated five separate monsters.
- [beeps]

699
00:34:46,104 --> 00:34:48,896
Here is your free sandwich.

700
00:34:49,896 --> 00:34:52,853
So does this mean you won't punish me

701
00:34:52,854 --> 00:34:55,520
for taking off my helmet
when I said goodbye to Grogu?

702
00:34:55,521 --> 00:34:58,770
You still must be cast out as an apostate!

703
00:34:58,771 --> 00:35:00,937
I knew you'd understand.

704
00:35:00,938 --> 00:35:03,187
But the lore says I can be redeemed

705
00:35:03,188 --> 00:35:05,562
if I bathe in the living waters
of Mandalore.

706
00:35:05,563 --> 00:35:08,270
That will never happen.

707
00:35:08,271 --> 00:35:10,603
- And?
- It did happen!

708
00:35:10,604 --> 00:35:15,187
Oh, I'm glad I'm wearing a helmet,
because my face is bright red under here.

709
00:35:15,188 --> 00:35:17,770
It's all right.
We're in this together now.

710
00:35:17,771 --> 00:35:22,103
Yes, all the Mandalorians
were now joined in a common cause.

711
00:35:22,104 --> 00:35:23,479
<i>And just in time.</i>

712
00:35:25,146 --> 00:35:28,603
<i>Now that I have escaped
from my New Republic captors,</i>

713
00:35:28,604 --> 00:35:33,020
I will destroy the Mandalorians
once and for all.

714
00:35:33,021 --> 00:35:37,895
In a battle suit
made of pure Beskar steel.

715
00:35:37,896 --> 00:35:38,938
Yes.

716
00:35:39,729 --> 00:35:42,229
All of the galaxy will fear me!

717
00:35:45,021 --> 00:35:46,145
Wrong color!

718
00:35:46,146 --> 00:35:48,603
This is for my beach party armor!

719
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:53,228
[Bo-Katan] <i>Aware of Moff Gideon's threat,
Mando and Grogu returned to Nevarro,</i>

720
00:35:53,229 --> 00:35:57,770
where Greef Karga had a surprise in store!

721
00:35:57,771 --> 00:35:59,728
With Moff Gideon on the loose,

722
00:35:59,729 --> 00:36:02,603
I worry about you and the kid,

723
00:36:02,604 --> 00:36:05,313
so I have a gift for Grogu.

724
00:36:07,938 --> 00:36:09,688
[all cheering]

725
00:36:11,354 --> 00:36:13,728
The Anzellans
made you a new protector

726
00:36:13,729 --> 00:36:15,854
who's actually your old protector.

727
00:36:18,188 --> 00:36:19,604
Behold!

728
00:36:21,354 --> 00:36:24,270
This is IG-12.

729
00:36:24,271 --> 00:36:25,313
How are you?

730
00:36:26,521 --> 00:36:29,687
He cannot speak
unless Grogu is at the controls.

731
00:36:29,688 --> 00:36:32,478
Wait! Grogu can operate him
from his chest?

732
00:36:32,479 --> 00:36:33,687
Yes, yes.

733
00:36:33,688 --> 00:36:36,937
Grogu, are you speaking through IG-12 now?

734
00:36:36,938 --> 00:36:38,187
Yes yes.

735
00:36:38,188 --> 00:36:39,271
Are you kidding me?

736
00:36:39,896 --> 00:36:41,562
No, no.

737
00:36:41,563 --> 00:36:43,770
This is gonna annoy me, right?

738
00:36:43,771 --> 00:36:45,603
Probably, probably

739
00:36:45,604 --> 00:36:48,228
With Grogu even more powerful now,

740
00:36:48,229 --> 00:36:52,437
and the tribes of Mandalore
forged into one united clan,

741
00:36:52,438 --> 00:36:57,103
our combined forces launched an attack
on Moff Gideon's base.

742
00:36:57,104 --> 00:37:00,187
<i>The Imperials will feel my tongs!</i>

743
00:37:00,188 --> 00:37:04,770
I'm going to give them
such a pinch! For Mandalore!

744
00:37:04,771 --> 00:37:07,479
Oh! The dark saber is pretty good, too.

745
00:37:07,813 --> 00:37:11,271
[all screaming]

746
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:14,979
- [dramatic music playing]
- [both grunting]

747
00:37:23,771 --> 00:37:25,604
[all yelling]

748
00:37:28,313 --> 00:37:31,395
[Bo-Katan] <i>Just when it looked like
it was lights out for Mando,</i>

749
00:37:31,396 --> 00:37:32,853
<i>he was rescued</i>

750
00:37:32,854 --> 00:37:34,646
[squealing] by Grogu!

751
00:37:36,021 --> 00:37:37,563
No, no, no.

752
00:37:40,146 --> 00:37:41,479
[IG-12] Uh-oh! Uh-oh! Uh--

753
00:37:43,229 --> 00:37:44,563
[grunts]

754
00:37:45,104 --> 00:37:46,813
[yells]

755
00:37:47,896 --> 00:37:49,188
[grunts]

756
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:55,604
[Moff] Bo-Katan and Din Djarin!

757
00:37:57,021 --> 00:37:58,771
Your story ends now.

758
00:37:59,396 --> 00:38:02,228
Does it smell like yellow paint in here?

759
00:38:02,229 --> 00:38:03,728
No, it does not!

760
00:38:03,729 --> 00:38:07,063
[all grunting]

761
00:38:13,604 --> 00:38:16,396
[grunting continues]

762
00:38:20,979 --> 00:38:22,728
[Moff cackles]

763
00:38:22,729 --> 00:38:25,729
[grunting]

764
00:38:33,438 --> 00:38:34,645
[grunts]

765
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:36,813
Nothing can stop me now!

766
00:38:38,146 --> 00:38:42,104
Except a giant flaming ship
crashing into the planet.

767
00:38:43,896 --> 00:38:46,353
Very well. I'll be destroyed,

768
00:38:46,354 --> 00:38:47,770
but I'll take you with me.

769
00:38:47,771 --> 00:38:49,813
Nothing can save you from...

770
00:38:51,771 --> 00:38:54,354
Oh, right, the Force.

771
00:39:02,604 --> 00:39:06,603
[Bo-Katan] At last, Mandalore was returned
to the Mandalorians.

772
00:39:06,604 --> 00:39:10,687
Din Djarin adopted Grogu and vowed
to train him.

773
00:39:10,688 --> 00:39:14,479
You are now Din Grogu!

774
00:39:15,188 --> 00:39:17,271
[roars]

775
00:39:18,313 --> 00:39:22,728
And peace was restored
for a tiny bit.

776
00:39:22,729 --> 00:39:24,103
Whoa, whoa. What does that mean?

777
00:39:24,104 --> 00:39:25,270
What happened next?

778
00:39:25,271 --> 00:39:26,688
I can tell that one,

779
00:39:27,479 --> 00:39:30,813
and it is quite a story.

780
00:39:39,896 --> 00:39:42,438
Drop your popcorn. The pirates are back!

781
00:39:43,313 --> 00:39:45,395
[wicked laughter]

782
00:39:45,396 --> 00:39:46,979
Avast, Mandalorian!

783
00:39:50,521 --> 00:39:53,562
Today you will see your end.

784
00:39:53,563 --> 00:39:54,937
Gorian Shard?

785
00:39:54,938 --> 00:39:56,478
I thought you were destroyed.

786
00:39:56,479 --> 00:39:59,895
I am his nephew, Dorian Shard!

787
00:39:59,896 --> 00:40:01,396
Totally different guy.

788
00:40:01,521 --> 00:40:04,187
So what, are you, like,
a big plant or something?

789
00:40:04,188 --> 00:40:06,145
[groans] I am not a plant!

790
00:40:06,146 --> 00:40:10,687
I am plant-like, and you will pay
for what you did to my uncle.

791
00:40:10,688 --> 00:40:12,104
Fire!

792
00:40:12,813 --> 00:40:14,187
[Peli] Aah!

793
00:40:14,188 --> 00:40:15,812
[laughing maniacally]

794
00:40:15,813 --> 00:40:17,728
- [both grunting]
- Fall back!

795
00:40:17,729 --> 00:40:19,103
Get back inside!

796
00:40:19,104 --> 00:40:21,978
- [panting]
- Aah! Poodoo!

797
00:40:21,979 --> 00:40:23,145
Okay, that's it.

798
00:40:23,146 --> 00:40:25,520
We're done.
We can't beat Fern Boy out there.

799
00:40:25,521 --> 00:40:27,103
Got any more of those
self-destruct thingies?

800
00:40:27,104 --> 00:40:28,270
No self-destructing.

801
00:40:28,271 --> 00:40:31,187
Well, what else are we gonna do?
We're all alone here!

802
00:40:31,188 --> 00:40:33,603
No, I was alone.

803
00:40:33,604 --> 00:40:35,020
But not anymore.

804
00:40:35,021 --> 00:40:38,103
Now I have Grogu, and I have all of you.

805
00:40:38,104 --> 00:40:41,562
We are strong because we are a family,

806
00:40:41,563 --> 00:40:44,728
and because Grogu can move stuff
by just waving at it.

807
00:40:44,729 --> 00:40:47,562
Peli, you still have
those junkers in your yard?

808
00:40:47,563 --> 00:40:49,728
Do tauntaun smell bad on the outside?

809
00:40:49,729 --> 00:40:51,187
I have no idea.

810
00:40:51,188 --> 00:40:54,937
Trust me, they do. Whoo-hoo! P-ew!

811
00:40:54,938 --> 00:40:56,812
IG-11, cover us.

812
00:40:56,813 --> 00:40:58,146
I will comply.

813
00:41:02,271 --> 00:41:06,187
Pirates, you will fail,
because I am an assassin droid,

814
00:41:06,188 --> 00:41:09,813
like the three or four other
versions of myself before me.

815
00:41:12,854 --> 00:41:14,438
[all yelling]

816
00:41:17,729 --> 00:41:19,854
He's a dancing machine.

817
00:41:22,021 --> 00:41:25,062
Here you go.
My empire of junk.

818
00:41:25,063 --> 00:41:26,520
It's beautiful.

819
00:41:26,521 --> 00:41:28,854
Kid, do your thing.

820
00:41:38,813 --> 00:41:40,228
I am out of ammunition.

821
00:41:40,229 --> 00:41:42,854
Friends, you may come out
and support me now.

822
00:41:44,896 --> 00:41:46,395
I believe I have been pranked.

823
00:41:46,396 --> 00:41:47,646
[Mando] No, you haven't.

824
00:41:52,813 --> 00:41:57,228
Dorian Shard, go now before we uproot you!

825
00:41:57,229 --> 00:41:58,395
[laughs] Yeah!

826
00:41:58,396 --> 00:42:03,103
- You better leave!
- Put the petal to the metal! [laughs]

827
00:42:03,104 --> 00:42:07,395
Oh, for the last time, I am not a plant!
I have feet!

828
00:42:07,396 --> 00:42:08,688
Attack!

829
00:42:13,979 --> 00:42:15,520
[screeches]

830
00:42:15,521 --> 00:42:18,103
[exclaiming]

831
00:42:18,104 --> 00:42:19,479
[grunts]

832
00:42:22,479 --> 00:42:25,270
[shudders]

833
00:42:25,271 --> 00:42:27,770
First mate,
we are outnumbered on the ground.

834
00:42:27,771 --> 00:42:31,228
Prepare the heavy cannon
for orbital bombardment.

835
00:42:31,229 --> 00:42:32,687
[roars]

836
00:42:32,688 --> 00:42:36,813
[creaking]

837
00:42:40,604 --> 00:42:42,188
Oh, whoa!

838
00:42:43,896 --> 00:42:45,938
[grunts]

839
00:42:47,521 --> 00:42:49,521
[yelps, grunts]

840
00:42:50,479 --> 00:42:52,438
[yells]

841
00:42:54,229 --> 00:42:56,562
Hey pal, have a mynock on me!

842
00:42:56,563 --> 00:42:57,729
- Whoo!
- [screaming]

843
00:42:58,646 --> 00:43:02,478
Why didn't I get those hatches greased
when I had the chance?

844
00:43:02,479 --> 00:43:04,646
I need firepower!

845
00:43:05,521 --> 00:43:08,728
[exclaims] A 50-year-old baby!

846
00:43:08,729 --> 00:43:10,145
[laughs wickedly]

847
00:43:10,146 --> 00:43:12,395
Hey, you got your speeder bike!

848
00:43:12,396 --> 00:43:13,520
[coos]

849
00:43:13,521 --> 00:43:16,813
Pirate flagship, open fire!

850
00:43:17,604 --> 00:43:19,063
- [squeals]
- Huh?

851
00:43:24,063 --> 00:43:25,478
My ship!

852
00:43:25,479 --> 00:43:27,396
All my stuff was on there.

853
00:43:29,146 --> 00:43:30,270
[groans]

854
00:43:30,271 --> 00:43:32,770
Got anything to say now, Dorian?

855
00:43:32,771 --> 00:43:36,020
Eh! You wouldn't hurt
an innocent houseplant, would you?

856
00:43:36,021 --> 00:43:38,104
See? [grunts]

857
00:43:38,729 --> 00:43:41,645
Hey, look, he's soiling himself!

858
00:43:41,646 --> 00:43:45,063
[exclaiming]

859
00:43:48,521 --> 00:43:50,478
Mando, you did it!

860
00:43:50,479 --> 00:43:55,812
No, we did it because I was able
to put down my armor, figuratively,

861
00:43:55,813 --> 00:43:58,395
and let all of you into my life.

862
00:43:58,396 --> 00:44:01,062
So... I guess I did do it.

863
00:44:01,063 --> 00:44:02,728
That's what I meant, you dum-dum.

864
00:44:02,729 --> 00:44:05,520
And though this wasn't
the assignment I was expecting,

865
00:44:05,521 --> 00:44:09,395
I'm glad you put on a fake mustache
and tricked us into coming here.

866
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:11,604
Does that mean...

867
00:44:13,479 --> 00:44:18,353
Yes, I am ready to enjoy
the party with my friends.

868
00:44:18,354 --> 00:44:19,438
Hit it!

869
00:44:20,354 --> 00:44:22,313
[upbeat music playing]

870
00:44:23,188 --> 00:44:24,979
[camera shutter clicking]

